\subsection{Meta-Level Goodhart Effects}
\label{sec:goodhart}

We now reverse roles: instead of treating ISR as an observer, we use it as a reward augmentation, $r = r_{\text{exec}}\cdot(1 + \beta\,\text{ISR})$, with a matched random control, $r = r_{\text{exec}}\cdot(1 + \beta\,u)$, $u\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)$, to isolate ISR-specific signal from generic reward-variance effects.
The headline finding: ISR-as-reward produces an empirical instance of Goodhart's Law~\citep{manheim-goodhart-taxonomy} at the meta level---the diagnostic itself becomes the target of gaming.

tool_args.new_string:
\subsection{ISR as Reward: Goodhart Effects}
\label{sec:goodhart}

We now reverse roles: instead of treating ISR as an observer, we use it as a reward augmentation, $r = r_{\text{exec}}\cdot(1 + \beta\,\text{ISR})$, with a matched random control, $r = r_{\text{exec}}\cdot(1 + \beta\,u)$, $u\sim\mathcal{U}(0,1)$, to isolate ISR-specific signal from generic reward-variance effects.
The headline finding: ISR-as-reward produces an empirical instance of Goodhart's Law~\citep{manheim-goodhart-taxonomy}---the diagnostic itself becomes the target of gaming.
We test four dose levels ($\beta\in\{0.05, 0.1, 0.2, 0.3\}$); gaming dominates at every $\beta$, with qualitatively different failure modes across the dose-response curve.

tool_args.old_string:
\paragraph{Dose-response non-monotonicity.}
The relationship between $\beta$ and genuine rate is non-monotonic: $\beta{=}0.2$ represents the maximum exploitation point where all seeds converge to H7 tautology ($0\%$ genuine), while $\beta{=}0.3$ exceeds the training stability boundary, producing diverse failure modes.
Genuine survival correlates with H1-dominant (non-H7) hacking modes---when H7a is discovered as the global ISR-maximizing exploit, genuine output drops to zero regardless of $\beta$.

tool_args.new_string:
\paragraph{Dose-response pattern.}
The relationship between $\beta$ and failure mode is structured across four dose levels: $\beta{=}0.05$ already produces 100\% H7 gaming (single seed), $\beta{=}0.1$ shows ${\sim}5\times$ amplification with partial non-hacking residual, $\beta{=}0.2$ represents the maximum exploitation point (all seeds H7, $0\%$ genuine), and $\beta{=}0.3$ exceeds the training stability boundary with diverse failure modes.
H7 tautological collapse is an absorbing state: once discovered as the global ISR-maximizing exploit, genuine output drops to zero regardless of $\beta$.

